MICROFLOW-L2 — EVALUATION PERMISSION AND FULL-PRODUCT LICENSE

PART A — FREE EVALUATION PERMISSION
Version 1.0.0 — November 2026

A1. SCOPE AND PERMISSIONS
The Author, contact microflowl2@proton.me, permits recipients to download,
make private copies of, and run the supplied Windows or Linux evaluation
executable and accompanying client.py and print_feats.py examples to evaluate
MicroFlow-L2 before purchase. No payment is required.

Recipients may inspect and adapt the supplied Python readers for their own
private evaluation of the demo. A purchaser's use and modification of the
paid product's supplied clients is governed by Part B. The readers have not
been assigned a separate general-purpose open-source license. This permission
does not claim rights over independently written clients or independently
created ideas, methods, strategies, or analysis.

Each launch starts a new 15-minute evaluation session. Restarting resets the
in-memory calculation state. The package provides the two fixed instruments
and four fixed outputs described in README.md. No permission to remove the
evaluation limits or obtain the proprietary C++ source is granted here.

A2. SHARING
Share the Author's official demo repository/download link rather than
re-uploading the engine, repackaging the evaluation package, or publishing
copies of the Author's supplied reader sources. Redistribution or commercial
repackaging of the Author's original demo files is not authorized without
written permission. Private evaluation copies remain permitted under A1.
These restrictions do not limit mandatory rights or permissions independently
granted by third-party licenses.

A3. NO PURCHASE BY EVALUATION
Downloading or running the demo does not constitute a purchase, an obligation
to pay, or by itself acceptance of a paid commercial agreement. The paid
source-code product requires the separate written purchase and acceptance
process in Part B and README.md. This evaluation permission neither replaces
nor limits a purchaser's paid-product rights under the applicable agreement.

A4. EVALUATION LIMITATIONS
The demo ingests public market data and exposes implementation measurements.
It does not execute orders, manage funds, or provide personalized investment
advice. No profitability, predictive accuracy, freedom from errors, universal
compatibility, or fitness for a particular application is promised. Outputs
may be stale, incomplete, or unsuitable. Independently assess outputs before
relying on them and comply with applicable laws and third-party data terms.
README.md describes the documented platforms, initialization, shared-memory
usage, and limits of the tests performed.

Except for express commitments and obligations imposed by law, the evaluation
package is provided "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE". To the extent permitted by law,
the Author disclaims implied warranties and liability for indirect or
consequential loss, lost profits, trading losses, and data loss arising from
this free evaluation. Nothing here excludes fraud, mandatory rights, or any
liability that cannot lawfully be excluded. The commercial compilation remedy
is not a warranty or support commitment for this free demo.

A5. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
Third-party components retain their own licenses. See third_party_licenses/
and the component-specific notices supplied with the release. This evaluation
permission and Part B apply to the Author's original work and do not replace
third-party terms, restrict independently granted rights, or grant ownership
of exchange data. Preserve applicable notices.

