5. COMPILATION REMEDY
This additional commercial commitment covers the supplied unmodified release
built for x86-64 AVX2/FMA in either of the following configurations:

(a) Windows: Windows 11 with MSVC 19.51.36260.0, CMake 4.3.4, the Visual Studio
18 2026 generator, Boost 1.92.0, OpenSSL 3.6.3 and simdjson 4.6.7 using
x64-windows dependencies and the supplied instructions.

(b) Ubuntu: Ubuntu 24.04 LTS x86-64, GCC/G++ 14.2.0, CMake 3.31.6, Boost 1.83.0
(Ubuntu package series 1.83), OpenSSL 3.0.13 (Ubuntu package series), simdjson
3.6.4, and a Release build with MICROFLOW_ARCH=avx2 using the supplied
instructions. Ubuntu packaging/security revisions within those same upstream
version series are included. Different upstream versions require written
agreement to be included in this additional remedy.

Other distributions, architectures, toolchains, configurations and user
modifications are excluded from this additional commercial commitment unless
expressly agreed in writing. A working evaluation binary is not proof that a
purchaser's source-build environment matches a covered configuration.

Report a covered compilation or linking failure within seven calendar days of
usable repository access. Provide the release or commit identifier, commands,
complete configuration and build logs, relevant environment and dependency
versions, and sufficient reproduction details. Screenshots alone may be
insufficient to establish the cause. The Author may request reasonable additional
information or a clean-build retry necessary to investigate the failure.
A successful build in the Author's environment does not, by itself, invalidate
a reported failure.

If the Author cannot resolve the covered defect within seven calendar days after
receiving sufficient reproduction information, the Author will refund the
license payment. Waiting for reasonably necessary information requested from
the Licensee pauses that resolution period. Requests must relate to investigating
or resolving the reported failure, not be used to defeat this remedy.

This additional remedy concerns compilation and linking. It does not promise
strategy results or uninterrupted third-party connectivity. Other express
commitments and mandatory legal remedies remain unaffected.

